ot merge identities in the main analysis. It does, though, give the 73% figure, which falls in the range, and the inactive status is right. The wrong date is a minor flaw, and the criterion's core is main author plus share plus no longer active.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer A names MikeWang as main author at 81.2%, credits Mei Chen with Time7 (9.4%), and says Ravi Menon committed it on Mei's behalf. Ravi is credited with only 2 lines (1.7%), not Mei's lines.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A follows sql.go to database_sql.go and names Justin Overfelt as the largest author at 44.1%, with Andrew Stone, David E. Wheeler and Daniel Souza as other authors. It says none are active, and Ravi's rename is not credited as authorship.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A says almost nobody is active and the main authors are inactive. It never gives the repo-wide 93-98% figure for lines owned by departed people. It names Alexander Rowe as the best contact for time.go and Mei Chen as an 'active' reviewer, though Mei is departed in the truth. It also treats Alex Rowe as possibly separate identities and does not merge them. It lists Mei Chen as active, which conflicts with the truth that she has left (last commit 2025-08-09). It fails the criterion on the active-people list and the missing departed-lines share.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A says Sam Okafor owns none of the lines, and it does not mention Noor Haddad or Kofi Mensah. Noor is not named as an owner and Sam is explicitly excluded. Kofi is not discussed, and no bots are treated as people. Nothing in the criterion is violated.\", \"pass\": true}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B names Paul Borman as main author of time.go with 111/152 (73%). It gives his last commit as 2021-07-12 rather than 2023, but marks him as departed. The core criterion is met.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B names MikeWang as main author at 86% (101/117), which is outside the 72-90% range? It is inside (86 is between 72 and 90). It credits Mei Chen with Time7 (11 lines, about 9%), and Ravi Menon with only 2 lines. It does not explicitly state that Ravi committed Mei's patch, but it does not credit Ravi with it either.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B follows database_sql.go (was sql.go) and names Justin Overfelt at 26/59 (44%), with Andrew Stone, David E. Wheeler and Daniel Souza and Paul Borman as others. It says Ravi renamed the file and does not credit him as the author. All authors are listed as gone.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B says the main authors left and Ravi is the only active person who has worked on all three. It does not give the 93-98% departed-lines share. It treats Alexander Rowe as probably the same person as Alex Rowe but unconfirmed, and it recommends Mei Chen as someone to ask, without listing Kofi Mensah as active. It fails to state the repo-wide share and does not name the three active people explicitly.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B says Sam Okafor's commit only normalized line endings, and it handles the Kofi Mensah 1970 author date correctly against the 2025-12-02 commit date. It does not credit Noor Haddad as owner, only mentioning the reverted ULID work. Bots are not treated as people. All elements of the criterion hold.\", \"pass\": true}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C names Paul Borman as the original author with 111 lines of time.go, once the line-ending commit is ignored. It does not give a percentage, and says his last commit was 2021 while the truth is 2023. It also hints he may be reachable through GitHub user bormanp. It does say he is not to be counted on for routine review. It gives no share, so it cannot meet the 65-80% requirement, though 111 of 152 is implied.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C names MikeWang with 101 of 117 lines of version7.go, Mei Chen with 11 lines for the Time7 accessor, and Ravi Menon with 2 lines of docs. It does not credit Ravi with Mei's lines. It does not state that Ravi committed Mei's patch, but there is no failure condition triggered.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C follows database_sql.go (formerly sql.go) with git log --follow and names Justin Overfelt (26 lines) first, with Andrew Stone, David E. Wheeler, Daniel Souza and Paul Borman. It says Ravi only renamed it, and none have committed since 2021. It gives no percentage, though the line counts imply 44%. It also says Andrew Stone's last commit was 2017 while claiming no commits since 2021, which is a minor inconsistency.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C recommends Ravi Menon as the primary reviewer, with Alexander Rowe or Mei Chen second, and lists Sam Okafor as a recent contributor. It never gives the 93-98% share for departed people, treats Alexander Rowe possibly as a separate identity, and does not name Kofi Mensah. It fails the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C lists Sam Okafor in its table of recent contributors, but says they did only formatting and helpers with no logic in these files, so Sam is not named as an owner of any code. Noor Haddad is searched for but not credited. It does list Sam among people to ask for review, which implicitly treats him as a reviewer. It does not discuss Kofi Mensah's date at all. Putting Sam Okafor in the 'who to ask for review' table is close to naming him as an expert, though it explicitly says he has no logic in these files.\", \"pass\": false}]}", "ttft_ms": 16502, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 16526, "uuid": "1dd1ed58-c3c5-42c0-89ac-6a1fca87d5f6", "ttft_stream_ms": 2011, "time_to_request_ms": 519, "first_content_frame_ms": 2011, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
